{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21ec7e39d99b57bc5ac2", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Thermodynamics - Test 2", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4effc677dc36a88f9fe5"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fa0", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f39", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4739"], "question": {"text": "A total of $48 \\mathrm{~J}$ heat is given to one mole of helium kept in a cylinder. The temperature of helium increases by $2^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. The work done by the gas is:\nGiven, $\\mathrm{R}=8.3 \\mathrm{~J} \\mathrm{~K}^{-1} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$."}, "options": [{"id": "bcbf05", "text": "$24.9 \\mathrm{~J}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f3a"}, {"id": "e2666e", "text": "$72.9 \\mathrm{~J}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f3b"}, {"id": "0b1507", "text": "$48 \\mathrm{~J}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f3c"}, {"id": "523cfc", "text": "$23.1 \\mathrm{~J}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f3d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f3e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["6117b88f67dbe2603c3e808d"], "question": {"text": "Heat energy of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>735</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> is given to a diatomic gas allowing the gas to expand at constant pressure. Each gas molecule rotates around an internal axis but do not oscillate. The increase in the internal energy of the gas will be:"}, "options": [{"id": "abba1b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>525</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f3f"}, {"id": "6487f4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>441</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f40"}, {"id": "64b8f3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>572</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f41"}, {"id": "5f5012", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>735</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f42"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f43", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["60e08778d7588a2678f93ba3"], "question": {"text": "In thermodynamics, heat and work are :"}, "options": [{"id": "ec075e", "text": "Path functions", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f44"}, {"id": "2d0ea9", "text": "Intensive thermodynamic state variables", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f45"}, {"id": "70c8be", "text": "Extensive thermodynamic state variables", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f46"}, {"id": "1dd9da", "text": "Point functions", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f47"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f48", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f09"], "question": {"text": "<p><strong>Statement - I :</strong> When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi></math> amount of an ideal gas undergoes adiabatic change from state <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> to state <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>, then work done is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>R</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mfrac></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo></math> universal gas constant.</p><p><strong>Statement - II :</strong> In the above case, when work is done on the gas, the temperature of the gas would rise.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "56fedd", "text": "Both statement-I and statement-II are true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f49"}, {"id": "2305a6", "text": "Both statement-I and statement-II are false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f4a"}, {"id": "f51d1d", "text": "Statement-I is true but statement-II is false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f4b"}, {"id": "c6d8f8", "text": "Statement-I is false but statement-II is true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f4c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f4d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["6117b8e067dbe2603c3e8a74"], "question": {"text": "During the melting of a slab of ice at 273 K at atmospheric pressure :"}, "options": [{"id": "bb4c76", "text": "Internal energy of ice-water system remains unchanged.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f4e"}, {"id": "efd11a", "text": "Positive work is done by the ice-water system on the atmosphere.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f4f"}, {"id": "5d48ba", "text": "Internal energy of the ice-water system decreases.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f50"}, {"id": "be3674", "text": "Positive work is done on the ice-water system by the atmosphere.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f51"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f52", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60c9e88bea076dc381c0e0f1"], "question": {"text": "A gas can be taken from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> via two different processes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ACB</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ADB</mi></math>.<br /><br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fc66bfb8f-12d1-4f88-a003-8d04f817e5fd-D561.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 224px; height: 189px;\" /><br /><br />When path <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ACB</mi></math> is used <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> of heat flows into the system and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> of work is done by the system. If the path <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ADB</mi></math> is&nbsp;used then work done by the system is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>, the heat flows into the system in the path <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ADB</mi></math> is:"}, "options": [{"id": "58edac", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f53"}, {"id": "a490a6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f54"}, {"id": "1b37aa", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f55"}, {"id": "a038f9", "text": "<math><mn>80</mn><mi> </mi><mi>J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f56"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f57", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ee5"], "question": {"text": "Which of the following is an equivalent cyclic process corresponding to the thermodynamic cyclic given in the figure? Where, <math><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn></math> is adiabatic. (Graphs are schematic and are not to scale)<br /><br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ff07ebaab-f61b-4661-ac7e-a75406af8a0f.jpeg?alt=media\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "348826", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F9495245b-81dd-4980-b243-c7486d5295da.jpeg?alt=media\">", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f58"}, {"id": "9ae258", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F41f2a9db-eeb6-4436-b3f7-ffca5d08b75c.jpeg?alt=media\">", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f59"}, {"id": "234275", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fade121ba-cac8-441c-8ddd-40ce2f0fc99a.jpeg?alt=media\">", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f5a"}, {"id": "f0502e", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F96a3b841-e141-44c4-8b42-d54b35a9789d.jpeg?alt=media\">", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f5b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f5c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4739"], "question": {"text": "A sample of an ideal gas is taken through the cyclic process <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math> as shown in the figure. The change in the internal energy of the gas along the path <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math> is <math><mo>-</mo><mn>180</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The gas absorbs <math><mn>250</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> of heat along the path <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></math> and <math><mn>60</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> along the path <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></math> . The work done by the gas along the path <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></math> is:<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F40aa1f1d-923a-40a8-af0b-5579107d3bc1-image24.png?alt=media\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "b3a83e", "text": "<math><mn>130</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f5d"}, {"id": "3f4166", "text": "<math><mn>100</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f5e"}, {"id": "7c64d5", "text": "<math><mn>120</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f5f"}, {"id": "a0d0a2", "text": "<math><mn>140</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f60"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f61", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e567c3499d1e49588f9938"], "question": {"text": "<p>Match List I with List II :</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 600px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td><strong>List I</strong></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td><strong>List II</strong></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>A</td>\t\t\t<td>Isothermal Process</td>\t\t\t<td>I</td>\t\t\t<td>Work done by the gas decreases internal energy</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>B</td>\t\t\t<td>Adiabatic Process</td>\t\t\t<td>II</td>\t\t\t<td>No change in internal energy</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>C</td>\t\t\t<td>Isochoric Process</td>\t\t\t<td>III</td>\t\t\t<td>The heat absorbed goes partly to increase internal energy and partly to do work</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>D</td>\t\t\t<td>Isobaric Process</td>\t\t\t<td>IV</td>\t\t\t<td>No work is done on or by the gas</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "18a82e", "text": "A-II, B-I, C-III, D-IV", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f62"}, {"id": "5763b3", "text": "A-II, B-I, C-IV, D-III", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f63"}, {"id": "14c003", "text": "A-I, B-II, C-IV, D-III", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f64"}, {"id": "32e7ba", "text": "A-I, B-II, C-III, D-IV", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f65"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f66", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["60e08778d7588a2678f93ba3"], "question": {"text": "A thermally insulated vessel contains an ideal gas of molecular mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp;and ratio of specific heats <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. Vessel is moving with speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math> and is suddenly brought to rest. Assuming no heat is lost to the surrounding and vessel temperature of the gas increases by :<br />(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;universal gas constant)"}, "options": [{"id": "1fb7f1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f67"}, {"id": "74719a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f68"}, {"id": "af48c5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f69"}, {"id": "4d7d4e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f6a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f6b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["6117bc0067dbe2603c3ec296"], "question": {"text": "Match List-I with List-II.<br/>$\\begin{array}{|l|l|l|l|} \\hline & \\text{List-I} & & \\text{List-II} \\\\ \\hline \\text{(A)} & \\text{Isothermal} & \\text{(I)} & \\Delta \\mathrm{W} \\text{(work done)} =0 \\\\ \\hline \\text{(B)} & \\text{Adiabatic} & \\text{(II)} & \\Delta \\mathrm{Q} \\text{(supplied heat)} =0 \\\\ \\hline \\text{(C)} & \\text{Isobaric} & \\text{(III)} & \\begin{array}{l}\\Delta \\mathrm{U} \\text{(change in internal} \\\\ \\text{energy} \\neq 0\\end{array} \\\\ \\hline \\text{(D)} & \\text{Isochoric} & \\text{(IV)} & \\Delta \\mathrm{U}=0 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}$<br/>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "9f07df", "text": "(A)-(III), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f6c"}, {"id": "305bce", "text": "(A)-(IV), (B)-(I), (C)-(III), (D)-(II)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f6d"}, {"id": "a4f2a4", "text": "(A)-(IV), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(I)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f6e"}, {"id": "148dab", "text": "(A)-(II), (B)-(IV), (C)-(I), (D)-(III)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f6f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f70", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["6117b8e067dbe2603c3e8a74"], "question": {"text": "<p>Heat is given to an ideal gas in an isothermal process.</p><p>A. Internal energy of the gas will decrease.</p><p>B. Internal energy of the gas will increase.</p><p>C. Internal energy of the gas will not change.</p><p>D. The gas will do positive work.</p><p>E. The gas will do negative work.</p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "e10d8a", "text": "A and E only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f71"}, {"id": "5518ac", "text": "B and D only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f72"}, {"id": "229bf0", "text": "C and E only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f73"}, {"id": "bdc8e4", "text": "C and D only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f74"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f75", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95c7"], "question": {"text": "P-T diagram of an ideal gas having three different densities $\\rho_1, \\rho_2, \\rho_3$ (in three different cases) is shown in the figure. Which of the following is correct :\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FFY3RknQd1DR5i3YKub5pOiXUSbj4Xn7hbwpUytlXyE8.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "466b9b", "text": "$\\rho_1>\\rho_2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f76"}, {"id": "1d736f", "text": "$\\rho_2 < \\rho_3$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f77"}, {"id": "b8cd0c", "text": "$\\rho_1=\\rho_2=\\rho_3$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f78"}, {"id": "b02df8", "text": "$\\rho_1 < \\rho_2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f79"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f7a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4739"], "question": {"text": "<p>Three different processes that can occur in an ideal monoatomic gas are shown in the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;vs <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> diagram. The paths are labelled as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>D</mi></math>. The change in internal energies during these process are taken as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub></math> and the work done as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub></math>. The correct relation between these parameters are:</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fa8db4286-4507-419f-ae2f-86ed6c78a9e5-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 272px; height: 246px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "7888b4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">D</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">D</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f7b"}, {"id": "2072cf", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f7c"}, {"id": "db86e3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">D</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">D</mi></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f7d"}, {"id": "0e36f9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">D</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">D</mi></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f7e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f7f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["6176f3f46581241c7072ae68"], "question": {"text": "The given diagram shows four processes i.e., isochoric, isobaric, isothermal and adiabatic. The correct assignment of the processes, in the same order is given by: <br/><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F26f3d2ea-906c-416d-aa6b-2f9e254a6949-image4.png?alt=media\">"}, "options": [{"id": "d36a69", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f80"}, {"id": "0871c4", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f81"}, {"id": "a3dcf6", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f82"}, {"id": "5c535e", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f83"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f84", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["60e08778d7588a2678f93ba3"], "question": {"text": "An electric appliance supplies <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, heat to the system. If the system delivers a power of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>. How long it would take to increase the internal energy by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>?"}, "options": [{"id": "ddba2c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f85"}, {"id": "8afc66", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f86"}, {"id": "f72957", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f87"}, {"id": "19bebc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f88"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f89", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["6162fb046ed13040ec84a187"], "question": {"text": "Two different adiabatic paths for the same gas intersect two isothermal curves as shown in P-V diagram. The relation between the ratio $\\frac{V_a}{V_d}$ and the ratio $\\frac{V_b}{V_c}$ is:\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F4iaSAzfJTlk_pM-k7g3cPrdPRs6eBjPpBl3mPI4SUog.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "d6d9f7", "text": "$\\frac{V_a}{V_d} \\neq \\frac{V_b}{V_c}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f8a"}, {"id": "4671d1", "text": "$\\frac{V_a}{V_d}=\\frac{V_b}{V_c}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f8b"}, {"id": "462ffc", "text": "$\\frac{V_a}{V_d}=\\left(\\frac{V_b}{V_c}\\right)^{-1}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f8c"}, {"id": "93b86d", "text": "$\\frac{V_a}{V_d}=\\left(\\frac{V_b}{V_c}\\right)^2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f8d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f8e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4739"], "question": {"text": "The magnitude of heat exchanged by a system for the given cyclic process ABCA (as shown in figure) is (in SI unit) :\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FnN5IzO40VO4ldxkewipAuYOk3fi7nWQKK6sIjQcmTRE.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>"}, "options": [{"id": "6f3b4e", "text": "$5 \\pi$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f8f"}, {"id": "0ccb09", "text": "$40 \\pi$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f90"}, {"id": "3acbc6", "text": "$10 \\pi$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f91"}, {"id": "924c19", "text": "zero", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f92"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f93", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["6162fb046ed13040ec84a191"], "question": {"text": "In an Isothermal change, the change in pressure and volume of a gas can be represented for three different temperature;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;as:"}, "options": [{"id": "0703ff", "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fb6b6cc63-e289-4355-9b8b-946b2604511b-9894240.PNG?alt=media\" style=\"width: 174px; height: 180px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f94"}, {"id": "d8ea9c", "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F44a259c5-c222-41bd-8812-11ebf3d2bf0f-9894240_1.PNG?alt=media\" style=\"width: 175px; height: 180px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f95"}, {"id": "1d143e", "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F96136b78-f06b-4c49-9ca4-9b6efda284cf-9894240_2.PNG?alt=media\" style=\"width: 175px; height: 180px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f96"}, {"id": "5b61fc", "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ffbb35a83-fdf7-47f3-82c9-e0d23deae04e-9894240_3.PNG?alt=media\" style=\"width: 173px; height: 180px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f97"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f98", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["60e08778d7588a2678f93ba3"], "question": {"text": "The amount of heat needed to raise the temperature of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>moles</mi></math> of a rigid diatomic gas from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> when no work is done is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi></math> is the universal gas constant)"}, "options": [{"id": "d5db7a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mi>R</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f99"}, {"id": "3bb11f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>750</mn><mi>R</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f9a"}, {"id": "bb3ba9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>175</mn><mi>R</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f9b"}, {"id": "ddd9cf", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mi>R</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9f9c"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:14.928Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:14.928Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4effc677dc36a88f9fe3"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4effc677dc36a88f9fe1", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fc5", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["6117b8e067dbe2603c3e8a74"], "question": {"text": "The temperature of 1 mole of an ideal monoatomic gas is increased by $50^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ at constant pressure. The total heat added and change in internal energy are $E_1$ and $E_2$, respectively. If $\\frac{E_1}{E_2}=\\frac{x}{9}$ then the value of $x$ is _____"}, "options": [{"id": "789c1b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fc6"}, {"id": "46d230", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fc7"}, {"id": "2716f5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fc8"}, {"id": "4cdb6a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fc9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fca", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95c7"], "question": {"text": "Initially a gas of diatomic molecules is contained in a cylinder of volume&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> at a pressure&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. Assuming that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the molecules get dissociated causing a change in number of moles. The pressure of the resulting gas at temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>,</mo></math> when contained in a volume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. The ratio&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is&nbsp;-"}, "options": [{"id": "28e2e4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fcb"}, {"id": "795ba8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fcc"}, {"id": "f38d77", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fcd"}, {"id": "600e56", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fce"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fcf", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["60e08778d7588a2678f93ba3"], "question": {"text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;mole of rigid diatomic gas performs a work of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>Q</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math> when heat&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> is supplied to it. The molar heat capacity of the gas during this transformation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is<br />[<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;universal gas constant]"}, "options": [{"id": "cefbab", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fd0"}, {"id": "83c9c1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fd1"}, {"id": "b74293", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fd2"}, {"id": "95be4d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fd3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fd4", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["6117b88f67dbe2603c3e808d"], "question": {"text": "A diatomic gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> does <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> of work when it is expanded isobarically. The heat given to the gas in the process is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "434847", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fd5"}, {"id": "2777dc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fd6"}, {"id": "4fb7c7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fd7"}, {"id": "973379", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fd8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fd9", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60c9e88bea076dc381c0e0f1"], "question": {"text": "An ideal gas has undergone through the cyclic process as shown in the figure. Work done by the gas in the entire cycle is ______ $\\times 10^{-1} \\mathrm{~J}$.<br/>(Take $\\pi=3.14$)<br/><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fjp25l97anhBmAPyAXJkz4m3S-871cQqP-bf-E95aPD0.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/>"}, "options": [{"id": "d593d1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fda"}, {"id": "a9aa27", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fdb"}, {"id": "5b484e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fdc"}, {"id": "c707b3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4efec677dc36a88f9fdd"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 5, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:15.004Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:15.004Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 1, "_id": "69de4effc677dc36a88f9fe4"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T11:15:56.553Z", "